<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Docker on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/docker/</link><description>Recent content in Docker on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 15:30:00 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/docker/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Generative Art with Context Free</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/contextfree-generative-art/</link><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 15:30:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/contextfree-generative-art/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;ve got a small repo, &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/ContextFree"&gt;ContextFree&lt;/a&gt;, that I keep coming back to whenever I want the specific kind of fun that comes from writing a handful of lines of code and having something unexpectedly pretty fall out the other end. It&amp;rsquo;s a collection of &lt;a href="https://www.contextfreeart.org/index.html"&gt;Context Free Art&lt;/a&gt; scripts — a tiny grammar for describing images as recursive drawing rules — plus a Docker image wrapping the &lt;a href="https://github.com/MtnViewJohn/context-free"&gt;&lt;code&gt;cfdg&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/a&gt; renderer so I can run them without installing anything locally.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Docker Images Again</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/dockertig/</link><pubDate>Wed, 06 Jul 2022 12:07:22 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/dockertig/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="devops-docker-images-again"&gt;Devops Docker images again&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Another Docker image with some tools useful for devops, this time includes the &lt;a href="https://jonas.github.io/tig/"&gt;TIG CLI utility&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="tig"&gt;Tig&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Tig Docker image &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/docker-tig"&gt;https://github.com/alastairhm/docker-tig&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;To use run the following;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h4 id="directly-on-the-cli"&gt;Directly on the CLI&lt;/h4&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="code-block"&gt;&#10; &lt;button class="code-copy" type="button" hidden aria-label="Copy code to clipboard"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="code-copy-label" aria-hidden="true"&gt;Copy&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/button&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;docker run --rm -ti -v &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;$(&lt;/span&gt;pwd&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;:/mnt ghcr.io/alastairhm/docker-tig:latest&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4 id="as-an-alias"&gt;As an alias&lt;/h4&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="code-block"&gt;&#10; &lt;button class="code-copy" type="button" hidden aria-label="Copy code to clipboard"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="code-copy-label" aria-hidden="true"&gt;Copy&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/button&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;alias tig&lt;span style="color:#f92672"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#e6db74"&gt;&amp;#39;docker run --rm -ti -v $(pwd):/mnt ghcr.io/alastairhm/docker-tig:latest&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;For full instructions on using TIG visit the &lt;a href="https://jonas.github.io/tig/doc/manual.html"&gt;offical instructions page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Docker Images</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/dockerimages/</link><pubDate>Wed, 29 Sep 2021 12:07:22 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/dockerimages/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="devops-docker-images"&gt;Devops Docker images&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;ve built a few Docker images with some tools useful for devops lately.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="spacevim"&gt;SpaceVim&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;SpaceVim Docker image with NeoVim &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/spacevim"&gt;https://github.com/alastairhm/spacevim&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="cfssl"&gt;CFSSL&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;CloudFlare&amp;rsquo;s SSL tools Docker image &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/docker-cfssl"&gt;https://github.com/alastairhm/docker-cfssl&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="terraform-security"&gt;Terraform Security&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;TFSec and TFLint tools Docker image &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/docker-terraform-check"&gt;https://github.com/alastairhm/docker-terraform-check&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="bitwarden-cli"&gt;Bitwarden CLI&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Bitwarden CLI tool Docker image &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/docker-bw"&gt;https://github.com/alastairhm/docker-bw&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>ympd - Control MPD player from a Docker Image</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/ympd-control-mpd-player-from-docker/</link><pubDate>Thu, 28 Apr 2016 12:24:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/ympd-control-mpd-player-from-docker/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 1 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 5 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;After setting up a Streaming radio instance of MPD/Icecast2 running in a &lt;a href="https://hub.docker.com/r/alastairhm/docker-icecast/" target="_blank"&gt;Docker image&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;I was looking for a nice front end to control it.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;I found &lt;a href="https://www.ympd.org/" target="_blank"&gt;ympd&lt;/a&gt; a MPD web GUI written in C, so created a Docker image to run it,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://hub.docker.com/r/alastairhm/docker-icecast/"&gt;https://hub.docker.com/r/alastairhm/docker-icecast/&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;it uses Alpine Linux so the image is only 6mb is size.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;You run it linking to your Docker image which is running MPD.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="background-color: #eaeef3; color: #333333; font-family: Consolas, 'Liberation Mono', Courier, monospace; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; white-space: pre;"&gt;docker run --name my-ympd -d -p 8080:8080 --link your_mpd_container:mpdhost alastair/docker-ympd&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Then browse to http://localhost:8080/&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;For more info checkout this &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/docker-ympd/blob/master/docker-compose.yml" target="_blank"&gt;Docker compose&lt;/a&gt; file which runs both my icecast and ympd images.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Docker Doku Wiki</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/docker-doku-wiki/</link><pubDate>Wed, 20 Apr 2016 15:27:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/docker-doku-wiki/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 1 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 13 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;Created a small footprint (less than 50mb) Docker image running the &lt;a href="https://www.dokuwiki.org/dokuwiki#" target="_blank"&gt;Doku Wiki&lt;/a&gt; on &lt;a href="https://www.lighttpd.net/" target="_blank"&gt;Lighttpd&lt;/a&gt; under &lt;a href="http://alpinelinux.org/" target="_blank"&gt;Alpine Linux&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Git Hub =&lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/alpine-doku" target="_blank"&gt; https://github.com/alastairhm/alpine-doku&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Docker Hub = &lt;a href="https://hub.docker.com/r/alastairhm/alpine-doku/"&gt;https://hub.docker.com/r/alastairhm/alpine-doku/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjOQqssteAzmQ_iIC6ubMWW4s5I1ICmrst2qqksT3EFREyjq8NvZDIIhDbj4xDqxBcTe0exnWCzg5dGVDUBORJJQqd6DTlVcutgelKuGjqrJmuQxXrmcxI5a0l74a1V1nvb_0OwRA7elV0/s1600/Screenshot%252B2016-04-20%252B03.24.18.png" imageanchor="1" style="margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"&gt;&lt;img border="0" height="177" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEjOQqssteAzmQ_iIC6ubMWW4s5I1ICmrst2qqksT3EFREyjq8NvZDIIhDbj4xDqxBcTe0exnWCzg5dGVDUBORJJQqd6DTlVcutgelKuGjqrJmuQxXrmcxI5a0l74a1V1nvb_0OwRA7elV0/s320/Screenshot%252B2016-04-20%252B03.24.18.png" width="320" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;h2&gt;&#10;Running&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="font-size: x-small;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Courier New&amp;quot;,Courier,monospace;"&gt;docker run --name "my-wiki" -d -p 80:80 alastairhm/alpine-doku&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Browse to install page &lt;a href="http://localhost/install.php"&gt;http://localhost/install.php&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Lighttpd and PHP running on Docker Example</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/lighttpd-and-php-running-on-docker/</link><pubDate>Mon, 18 Apr 2016 10:46:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/lighttpd-and-php-running-on-docker/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 1 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 7 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;Here is a low resource Lighttpd with PHP Docker image running on Alpine Linux, only ~37MB image.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Github = &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/alpine-lighttpd-php"&gt;https://github.com/alastairhm/alpine-lighttpd-php&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Docker Hub = &lt;a href="https://hub.docker.com/r/alastairhm/alpine-lighttpd-php/"&gt;https://hub.docker.com/r/alastairhm/alpine-lighttpd-php/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Create an example PHP file in your local directory&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;courier new&amp;quot; , &amp;quot;courier&amp;quot; , monospace;"&gt;echo "&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;courier new&amp;quot; , &amp;quot;courier&amp;quot; , monospace;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;courier new&amp;quot; , &amp;quot;courier&amp;quot; , monospace;"&gt;&amp;lt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;?php phpinfo(); ?&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;courier new&amp;quot; , &amp;quot;courier&amp;quot; , monospace;"&gt;&amp;gt;&lt;/span&gt;" &amp;gt;&amp;gt; index.php&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Then start the Docker image;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;courier new&amp;quot; , &amp;quot;courier&amp;quot; , monospace;"&gt;docker run --name "my-lighttpd-php" -p 8000:80 -v $(pwd):/var/www alastairhm/alpine-lighttpd-php&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;Browse to &lt;a href="http://localhost:8000/"&gt;http://localhost:8000/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEgYWIck0V67HWxjgOpScXap5OEx2vv1gBjwCgyvR6BLSFY6UyA9KmMkeljWAO1qYnEBfaLGbzGRqyNlYZ0EIJ32tlzMwcGqmdowivbjtawBEZDlxGBQ27AgmsnDVKpHsp3A3Ej5fhdmykU/s1600/Screenshot%252B2016-04-18%252B10.44.29.png" imageanchor="1" style="margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"&gt;&lt;img border="0" height="227" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEgYWIck0V67HWxjgOpScXap5OEx2vv1gBjwCgyvR6BLSFY6UyA9KmMkeljWAO1qYnEBfaLGbzGRqyNlYZ0EIJ32tlzMwcGqmdowivbjtawBEZDlxGBQ27AgmsnDVKpHsp3A3Ej5fhdmykU/s320/Screenshot%252B2016-04-18%252B10.44.29.png" width="320" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Docker OwnCloud Update</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/docker-owncloud-update/</link><pubDate>Wed, 13 Apr 2016 12:48:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/docker-owncloud-update/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;I've updated the owncloud Docker compose file to include a Nginx automatic reverse proxy and added some scripts to handle backing up and restoring the database.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;See more information in the &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/owncloud/blob/master/README.md" target="_blank"&gt;README&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle's Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Ghost Blog, Docker compose example</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/ghost-blog-docker-compose-example/</link><pubDate>Sat, 09 Apr 2016 17:01:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/ghost-blog-docker-compose-example/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 2 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 8 links are now broken — mostly dead 2008–2013 feed-syndication infrastructure (FeedBurner, Gawker, AOL&amp;rsquo;s old blog network, Pheedo, Yahoo Pipes). Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;article class="markdown-body entry-content" itemprop="text"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Docker Compose Tutorial&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Running through the Docker Compose tutorial on &lt;a href="http://www.linux.com/learn/tutorials/893685-introduction-to-docker-compose-tool-for-multi-container-applications/"&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.linux.com/learn/tutorials/893685-introduction-to-docker-compose-tool-for-multi-container-applications/"&gt;http://www.linux.com/learn/tutorials/893685-introduction-to-docker-compose-tool-for-multi-container-applications/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;This sets up a instance of &lt;a href="https://ghost.org/" target="_blank"&gt;Ghost&lt;/a&gt; micro blogging platform running in a Docker image connected to a MySQL Docker images.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;There are also a couple of scripts to backup and restore the MySQL database.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;b&gt;Useful pages&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://docs.docker.com/v1.5/compose/yml/"&gt;&lt;a href="https://docs.docker.com/v1.5/compose/yml/"&gt;https://docs.docker.com/v1.5/compose/yml/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Owncloud running on Docker</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/owncloud-running-on-docker/</link><pubDate>Sat, 09 Apr 2016 16:37:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/owncloud-running-on-docker/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="separator" style="clear: both; text-align: center;"&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEj8RKV82q4iv9LCHFP4oHyi9dmec8GCOJnOA0TxCxG0wjYYRpm2zwhXNBe-ju8bxF_LDf1PzbK80bCqLX6QyCrgxxuWlCFaGGt4Qj1vob0N2OSF7SfbqZmIUlgGUflSnYVkVUcQrxqU1bg/s1600/Screenshot%252B2016-04-09%252B04.33.41.png" imageanchor="1" style="margin-left: 1em; margin-right: 1em;"&gt;&lt;img border="0" height="194" src="https://blogger.googleusercontent.com/img/b/R29vZ2xl/AVvXsEj8RKV82q4iv9LCHFP4oHyi9dmec8GCOJnOA0TxCxG0wjYYRpm2zwhXNBe-ju8bxF_LDf1PzbK80bCqLX6QyCrgxxuWlCFaGGt4Qj1vob0N2OSF7SfbqZmIUlgGUflSnYVkVUcQrxqU1bg/s320/Screenshot%252B2016-04-09%252B04.33.41.png" width="320" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;h1&gt;&#10;&amp;nbsp;Owncloud Running on Docker&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;Just a quick test getting ownCloud to run on Docker&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;h2&gt;&#10;&lt;a class="anchor" href="https://github.com/alastairhm/owncloud#refences" id="user-content-refences"&gt;&lt;svg class="octicon octicon-link" height="16" viewbox="0 0 16 16" width="16"&gt;&lt;path d="M4 9h1v1h-1c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5s1.55-3.5 3-3.5h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-0.91 2.72-2 3.25v-1.16c0.58-0.45 1-1.27 1-2.09 0-1.28-1.02-2.5-2-2.5H4c-0.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5s1 2.5 2 2.5z m9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5s-1.02 2.5-2 2.5H9c-0.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-0.83 0.42-1.64 1-2.09v-1.16c-1.09 0.53-2 1.84-2 3.25 0 1.81 1.55 3.5 3 3.5h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5s-1.5-3.5-3-3.5z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Refences&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Owncloud Docker information : &lt;a href="https://hub.docker.com/r/library/owncloud/"&gt;https://hub.docker.com/r/library/owncloud/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;mySQL Docker information : &lt;a href="https://hub.docker.com/_/mysql/"&gt;https://hub.docker.com/_/mysql/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h2&gt;&#10;&lt;a class="anchor" href="https://github.com/alastairhm/owncloud#setup-the-database-connection" id="user-content-setup-the-database-connection"&gt;&lt;svg class="octicon octicon-link" height="16" viewbox="0 0 16 16" width="16"&gt;&lt;path d="M4 9h1v1h-1c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5s1.55-3.5 3-3.5h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-0.91 2.72-2 3.25v-1.16c0.58-0.45 1-1.27 1-2.09 0-1.28-1.02-2.5-2-2.5H4c-0.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5s1 2.5 2 2.5z m9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5s-1.02 2.5-2 2.5H9c-0.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-0.83 0.42-1.64 1-2.09v-1.16c-1.09 0.53-2 1.84-2 3.25 0 1.81 1.55 3.5 3 3.5h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5s-1.5-3.5-3-3.5z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Setup the database connection&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;Enter details as follows (as setup in the compose file);&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Choose MySQL/MariaDB&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Database user : owncloud&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Database password : password&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Database name : owncloud&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Host : mysql&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h2&gt;&#10;&lt;a class="anchor" href="https://github.com/alastairhm/owncloud#local-volume" id="user-content-local-volume"&gt;&lt;svg class="octicon octicon-link" height="16" viewbox="0 0 16 16" width="16"&gt;&lt;path d="M4 9h1v1h-1c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5s1.55-3.5 3-3.5h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-0.91 2.72-2 3.25v-1.16c0.58-0.45 1-1.27 1-2.09 0-1.28-1.02-2.5-2-2.5H4c-0.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5s1 2.5 2 2.5z m9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5s-1.02 2.5-2 2.5H9c-0.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-0.83 0.42-1.64 1-2.09v-1.16c-1.09 0.53-2 1.84-2 3.25 0 1.81 1.55 3.5 3 3.5h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5s-1.5-3.5-3-3.5z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Local Volume&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;Create a local directory for your ownCloud files /var/www/owncloud&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;h2&gt;&#10;&lt;a class="anchor" href="https://github.com/alastairhm/owncloud#running" id="user-content-running"&gt;&lt;svg class="octicon octicon-link" height="16" viewbox="0 0 16 16" width="16"&gt;&lt;path d="M4 9h1v1h-1c-1.5 0-3-1.69-3-3.5s1.55-3.5 3-3.5h4c1.45 0 3 1.69 3 3.5 0 1.41-0.91 2.72-2 3.25v-1.16c0.58-0.45 1-1.27 1-2.09 0-1.28-1.02-2.5-2-2.5H4c-0.98 0-2 1.22-2 2.5s1 2.5 2 2.5z m9-3h-1v1h1c1 0 2 1.22 2 2.5s-1.02 2.5-2 2.5H9c-0.98 0-2-1.22-2-2.5 0-0.83 0.42-1.64 1-2.09v-1.16c-1.09 0.53-2 1.84-2 3.25 0 1.81 1.55 3.5 3 3.5h4c1.45 0 3-1.69 3-3.5s-1.5-3.5-3-3.5z"&gt;&lt;/path&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Running&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;Clone the &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/owncloud" target="_blank"&gt;repo&lt;/a&gt; then run the following in the directory&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;docker-compose -d up&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Testing Docker Puppet Module</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/testing-docker-puppet-module/</link><pubDate>Wed, 04 Feb 2015 14:59:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/testing-docker-puppet-module/</guid><description>&lt;div dir="ltr" style="text-align: left;" trbidi="on"&gt;&#10;This module &lt;a href="https://github.com/garethr/garethr-docker"&gt;https://github.com/garethr/garethr-docker&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;lets you install and control Docker using Puppet.&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;For example this &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/docker.git" target="_blank"&gt;Vagrant setup&lt;/a&gt; spins up an Ubuntu VM and then using the Docker module spins up a Jenkins build server Docker container with a few simple commands;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;include docker&#10;docker::image { 'jenkins': }&#10;&lt;p&gt;docker::run { &amp;lsquo;some-jenkins&amp;rsquo;:&#10;image =&amp;gt; &amp;lsquo;jenkins&amp;rsquo;,&#10;ports =&amp;gt; &amp;lsquo;8080:8080&amp;rsquo;,&#10;volumes =&amp;gt; &amp;lsquo;/vagrant/jenkins&amp;rsquo;,&#10;use_name =&amp;gt; true,&#10;}&lt;/pre&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;br /&gt;&#10;&lt;a href="http://meekgonkey.blogspot.com/"&gt;Doodle&amp;rsquo;s Geek Monkey&lt;/a&gt; by &lt;a href="http://twitter.com/alastair_hm"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>